+GalaxyPlay — Third-party notices and licenses
+
+GalaxyPlay is an independently maintained CarPlay receiver for Galaxy L7. This document records source attribution, dependencies and resource rights. Complete license texts follow these notices. Source code and build instructions: https://github.com/Tamshen/GalaxyPlay
+
+Direct upstream
+
+DiPlay — GPL-3.0. Receiver protocol, connection and recovery code.
+https://github.com/shihabal3amri/DiPlay
+Original xcertplay source attribution and file licenses remain in the receiver sources.
+
+Runtime components
+
+Concentus 1.0.0 — BSD-3-Clause. Pure Java Opus encoder and decoder, published as com.plasmoverse:concentus:1.0.0. Software fallback for wireless audio and microphone streams when system Opus codecs cannot start; audio routing is unchanged. The original META-INF/LICENSE from the artifact is bundled as licenses/Concentus-LICENSE.txt.
+https://github.com/lostromb/concentus
+https://github.com/plasmoapp/concentus
+Integration maintenance: the codec algorithms come from Concentus; GalaxyPlay maintains capability detection, per-stream fallback and resource release.
+
+AndroidX — Apache-2.0. Android support components including Core, Activity, Lifecycle and Car App. Copyright notices remain with the respective Android Open Source Project sources.
+https://github.com/androidx/androidx
+
+Jetpack Compose — Apache-2.0. Declared UI, Graphics, Material 3 and tooling dependencies. The current L7 interface uses Android Views.
+https://github.com/androidx/androidx/tree/androidx-main/compose
+
+Kotlin — Apache-2.0. JetBrains standard library and compiler plugins.
+https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin
+
+Kotlin Coroutines — Apache-2.0. Coroutine support brought in by AndroidX.
+https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.coroutines
+
+Kotlin Serialization — Apache-2.0. Serialization core brought in by AndroidX.
+https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.serialization
+
+JetBrains Annotations — Apache-2.0. Nullability and code contract annotations.
+https://github.com/JetBrains/java-annotations
+
+Bouncy Castle — Bouncy Castle license (MIT style). Cryptography, certificates and key handling. Copyright The Legion of the Bouncy Castle Inc.; the complete accompanying notice follows.
+https://www.bouncycastle.org/about/license/
+
+JmDNS — Apache-2.0. mDNS / DNS-SD discovery.
+https://github.com/jmdns/jmdns
+
+SLF4J — MIT. Logging API brought in by JmDNS. Copyright QOS.ch; the complete accompanying notice follows.
+https://www.slf4j.org/license.html
+
+Guava — Apache-2.0. Java utilities and asynchronous support, including listenablefuture and failureaccess.
+https://github.com/google/guava
+
+JSpecify — Apache-2.0. Nullability annotations.
+https://github.com/jspecify/jspecify
+
+FindBugs JSR-305 annotations — Apache-2.0 for the jsr305 artifact brought in by Guava. This does not describe the license of the entire FindBugs project.
+https://github.com/findbugsproject/findbugs
+
+Checker Framework annotations — MIT for checker-qual. Other parts of the full checker project retain their own licenses.
+https://github.com/typetools/checker-framework
+
+Error Prone annotations — Apache-2.0. error_prone_annotations brought in by Guava.
+https://github.com/google/error-prone
+
+J2ObjC annotations — Apache-2.0. j2objc-annotations brought in by Guava.
+https://github.com/google/j2objc
+
+Build and test tools
+
+JUnit 4 — EPL-1.0. JVM tests; not an application runtime component.
+https://github.com/junit-team/junit4
+
+Robolectric — MIT, with Apache-2.0 notices for some files. Android component tests; not an application runtime component.
+https://github.com/robolectric/robolectric
+
+Mockito 5.20.0
+Source: https://github.com/mockito/mockito/tree/v5.20.0
+Purpose: Construction isolation for host window and reconnect unit tests; test-only, excluded from APK runtime dependencies.
+License: MIT; see licenses/Mockito-LICENSE.txt.
+
+Gradle — Apache-2.0. Build tasks and dependency resolution.
+https://github.com/gradle/gradle
+
+Android Gradle Plugin — Apache-2.0. Android compilation and packaging.
+https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/base/
+
+Gradle Foojay Toolchains — Apache-2.0. Java toolchain resolution. Downloaded JDK distributions have separate licenses.
+https://github.com/gradle/foojay-toolchains
+
+MobileDevOps Android SDK Image — MIT for the image project. Android SDK, NDK, JDK and other bundled components retain their own licenses.
+https://github.com/MobileDevOps/android-sdk-image
+
+Retained source notices
+
+DiAuto — AGPL-3.0-only source notice inherited through the DiPlay host files. The current home screen, settings and floating menus use GalaxyPlay native components with Flyme Auto reference styling. Existing source-file attribution and licenses remain. DiAuto is not included as a separate SDK, module or Gradle dependency.
+https://github.com/shihabal3amri/DiAuto
+
+Resources and branding
